1. THE STORY AND THE ART: ALL RIGHTS RESERVED

The story and the art of Dog Quest are the intellectual property of Andrew Mueller.
All rights reserved.

"The story" means the world, its history and lore, the characters and creatures, their
names and personalities, the plot, quests, mysteries and endings, and all of the writing
in the game: dialogue, narration, letters, journal pages, books, signs, songs, quest and
item text, and the names of people, places and things.

"The art" means every visual design in the game: characters, creatures, bosses, portraits,
buildings, rooms, furniture, places, maps, items, icons, effects and any other artwork,
whether it is stored as an image or drawn by code.

This covers in particular:
  - the writing and names inside game/src/ (above all game/src/06b_story.js) and game/body.html
  - the code that draws the art, including game/src/05_art.js, game/src/05b_creatures.js,
    game/src/05c_buildings.js, game/src/04_ground.js and the drawing functions in any other file
  - the built game (docs/index.html and any other build) taken as a whole
  - the game section of README.md

You may play the game at its official address and view this repository on GitHub. You may
not copy, modify, adapt, publish, distribute, sell or make derivative works from the story or
the art, in whole or in part, without written permission from Andrew Mueller.


